quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  4,15,"As for those of your women who commit an indecent act (i.e. adultery), produce against them four witnesses from among yourselves. If they testify, confine them to (their) homes until (natural) death completes their term of life, or Allah ordains a (different) course for them.*"
  4,16,"When two of you commit this (sin of adultery), punish them both. But if they repent and reform, then leave them alone. Indeed, Allah is Most Clement, All-Merciful."
  4,17,"Allah shall turn (in forgiveness) only towards those who commit evil out of ignorance and then repent soon after. They are the ones whom Allah will pardon. And Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise."
  4,18,"However, (the acceptance of) repentance is not for those who persist in committing sins until death approaches one of them, (and then) he says: ‘Now I repent’, nor for those who die as disbelievers. For such people, We have prepared a painful punishment."
  4,19,"O believers! It is not permissible for you to inherit women (of your deceased relatives) through coercion, nor should you mistreat them (or prevent them from remarrying) so that you may take away some of what you have given them (as a ransom for divorce) unless they commit gross indecency (i.e. adultery). Treat them honourably; if you dislike them, perhaps you hate something while Allah has placed abundant good in it."
